.TH mcx_strerror 3 (unknown-date) "mcxedit (unknown-version)"
.SH NAME
mcx_strerror \- get error string for mcxedit library

.SH LIBRARY
libmcx
.RI ( libmcx ,\~ \-lmcx )

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmcx/error.h>
.P
.BI "const char *mcx_strerror(int " code );

.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
.I code
should contain the error value, and may not be less than 0.
.P
This function invokes
.BR strerror (3)
for errors not specific to mcxedit.
This function will therefore work for standard C error codes.
All libmcx error codes are >0x1000, and shouldn't conflict with
any system codes.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the error string, or NULL if the error code was invalid.
This pointer does not need to be freed.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strerror (3),
.BR perror (3),
.BR printf (3),
.BR puts (3),
.BR err (3)
